tegic choice because it maximizes relative mobility (restricting the opponent's options) and creates a stable diagonal structure. Unlike (C,4), it prevents the opponent from playing at (B,3). Unlike (C,5) or (C,6), it maintains the integrity of my central cluster without allowing the opponent to immediately flip my key pieces at E4/E5.\n\nAnswer: (C, 3)"}
